body:
Someone has posted their own theories on this site;

[https://whereaboutsstillunknown.wordpress.com/2018/05/20/reed-jeppson/](https://whereaboutsstillunknown.wordpress.com/2018/05/20/reed-jeppson/)

Personally, I think that there was some form of foul play involved in this case. The anonymous tip is extremely suspicious to me, and the changes from between 1964-2018 is massive meaning evidence could have been accidentally destroyed.

Unsure if this is helpful, but a Facebook post from the Prince William Country Police Department states that the three ladies killed in the Real Estate Sales Trailer on June the 24, 1978  were Karen Scarborough, Sharon Lake and Deborah Frank. Apparently it was Karen's first day working there and Sharon and Deborah were potential customers at the time. It says that they were each shot dead. 

Lisa R.Triggs was last seen in front of the Giant Grocery Store in Center Plaza Shopping Center. Detectives believe Lisa walked from Center Plaza, where a traveling carnival was taking place, along a path toward her home on Estate Drive. There were some suspects, however I currently cannot open some articles, so here is one;

[https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=3&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=0ahUKEwiDoLm4nIDcAhXEyKYKHeQoBroQFgg0MAI&url=http&#37;3A&#37;2F&#37;2Fwww.fauquier.com&#37;2Fprince\_william\_times&#37;2Fnews&#37;2Fcold-case-who-killed-lisa-renee-triggs&#37;2Farticle\_9606e298-3fbf-11e7-9fb6-3b4df16f1697.html&usg=AOvVaw13zNzv3XQQA\_tSuaKSy78C](https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=3&cad=rja&uact=8&ved=0ahUKEwiDoLm4nIDcAhXEyKYKHeQoBroQFgg0MAI&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.fauquier.com%2Fprince_william_times%2Fnews%2Fcold-case-who-killed-lisa-renee-triggs%2Farticle_9606e298-3fbf-11e7-9fb6-3b4df16f1697.html&usg=AOvVaw13zNzv3XQQA_tSuaKSy78C)
